    "knowledge_point_id": "0c8f0fa1-a86a-577f-bdc9-fc7427faa18d",
    "knowledge_point": "Computing the Image of a Line Given by an Equation in Slope-Intercept Form",
    "problem": "Consider the line $y=4x+5$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T?$",
    "worked_solution": "First, notice that the line $y=4x+5$ passes through the points $G(0,5)$ and $H(1,9)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $G$ and $H$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -15 & -28\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${G}^{′}(0,-15)$ and ${H}^{′}(2,-28).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${G}^{′}$ and ${H}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-15) & =\\frac{-28-(-15)}{2-0}(x-0) \\\\ y+15 & =-\\frac{13}{2}x \\\\ 2y+30 & =-13x \\\\ 13x+2y+30 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
